      "writtenOn": "2018-08-24T22:57:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "ARMv6-M interrupt handlers are similar to ARMv7-M, in that they can be ordinary C functions.  \n\nSo, instead of fixing up the PC-relative address of exception_panic, the default_handler() can just be an ordinary C function that calls exception_panic().",
