      "writtenOn": "2018-08-25T03:15:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Will take a look into it, but I\u0027m OOO next week.\n\nI tried to be as conservative as possible due to the limited testing I could do myself and therefore kept things like the original as much as possible. Why was this written in assembly in the first place if they\u0027re C ABI compatible?\n\nSince we\u0027re just jumping into exception_panic, couldn\u0027t we define exception_panic as the default handler?",
